COMMENT     REFSEQ INFORMATION: The reference sequence is identical to
            AP011954.1.
            R621a carries a highly mobile DNA segment designated 'shufflon'.
            The DNA sequence presented below is that of one specific clone,
            which was fixed because of the lack of rci gene encoding
            shufflon-specific recombinase. The shufflon is thought to be a
            biological switch to select one of seven pilV genes encoding
            preadhesins in which N-tertminal region is constant, while
            C-terminal region is variable.
            The annotation was added by the NCBI Prokaryotic Genome Annotation
            Pipeline (PGAP). Information about PGAP can be found here:
            https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/genome/annotation_prok/
            
